      "text": "To find the total amount of money the pirate has accumulated, we need to convert each of the base-5 numbers to base-10 and then sum them up.\n\nFirst, let's convert \\(3124_5\\) to base-10. The number \\(3124_5\\) can be expanded as follows:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5^3 + 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0\n\\]\nCalculating each term individually:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4\n\\]\nAdding these values together gives:\n\\[\n375 + 25 + 10 + 4 = 414\n\\]\nSo, \\(3124_5 = 414_{10}\\).\n\nNext, let's convert \\(3122_5\\) to base-10. Using the same expansion method:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5^3 + 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 2 \\cdot 5^0\n\\]\nCalculating each term individually:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^0 = 2 \\cdot 1 = 2\n\\]\nAdding these values together gives:\n\\[\n375 + 25 + 10 + 2 = 412\n\\]\nSo, \\(3122_5 = 412_{10}\\).\n\nFinally, let's convert \\(124_5\\) to base-10. Using the same expansion method:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0\n\\]\nCalculating each term individually:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4\n\\]\nAdding these values together gives:\n\\[\n25 + 10 + 4 = 39\n\\]\nSo, \\(124_5 = 39_{10}\\).\n\nNow, we sum the base-10 equivalents of the three amounts:\n\\[\n414 + 412 + 39 = 865\n\\]\nTherefore, the total dollar amount that the pirate has accumulated is \\(\\boxed{865}\\).",
